{title: Not a Thread}
{subtitle: Genesis 14:1–4; 14:8–10; 14:11–12; 14:14–16; 14:17–21; 14:22–24}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 87}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm7] | [Abmaj7] |
| [Bbsus4] [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Four kings marched to war that [Cm7]day
Against the five in the val[Abmaj7]ley
Twelve years they served Che[Eb]dorlaomer [Bb]
[Eb]But in the thirteenth, they re[Cm7]belled
The Valley of Siddim had [Abmaj7]pits
Where kings of Sodom [Eb]fell
[Bb/D]The [Ab]goods of Sodom were [Bb]seized
And [Ab]Lot was taken a[Bb]way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]I raised [Bb/D]my hand to [Cm7]God Most High
Maker [Bb6]of heaven and [Abmaj7]earth
I will accept noth[Bb]ing from you
[Eb]Not a [Bb/D]thread or san[Cm7]dal strap
So you can [Bb6]never say
[Abmaj7]I made Abram [Bb]rich
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Three hundred eighteen men a[Cm7]rose
Born in Abram’s house[Abmaj7]hold
He pursued the army to [Eb]Dan
And [Bb]struck them by [Eb]night
He re[Bb/D]covered all the [Cm7]goods
And brought back Lot his [Abmaj7]kinsman
The king of Sodom came out
[Eb]To meet him [Bb]in the King’s [Abmaj7]Val[Bb]ley
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]I raised [Bb/D]my hand to [Cm7]God Most High
Maker [Bb]of heaven and [Abmaj7]earth
I will accept noth[Bb]ing from you
[Eb]Not a [Bb/D]thread or san[Cm7]dal strap
So you can [Bb]never say
[Abmaj7]I made Abram [Bb]rich
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Abmaj7]Aner, Eshcol, and Mamre
[Bb]Shall take their share [Cm7]of food
But Abram takes nothing [Gm]else
From the king’s greedy hand
[Abmaj7]His oath is strong and [Bb]true
Be[Abmaj7]fore the Maker of [Bb]all
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]I raised [Bb/D]my hand to [Cm7]God Most High
Maker [Bb]of heaven and [Abmaj7]earth
I will accept noth[Bb]ing from you
[Eb]Not a [Bb/D]thread or san[Cm7]dal strap
So you can [Bb]never say
[Abmaj7]I made Abram [Bb]rich [Eb][Bb/D][Cm7][Bb][Abmaj7]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Not a [Eb][Bb/D][Cm7]thread [Bb]
